  "final_message": "Task 1 is finished and recorded in the ledger. `task-done` accepted it on the first try.\n\n**Mutant step.** In the first mutant run, mutant 2 survived. That mutant gives the first person every leftover cent, and the plan's only test with a remainder, `split(1000, 3)`, leaves just one cent over, so the wrong version still passed. The spec sentence at `specs/split.md:9`, \"one each to the first people\", also covers the case where several cents are left over, and no test had that case.\n- I added a separate test for it, `test_the_first_people_pay_one_cent_each_of_several_left_over`, which checks that `split(1100, 3) == [367, 367, 366]`. Neither plan test was changed.\n- I committed it as `18613bd` with the trailers `Mutant-step: task 1 input shape` and `Mutant-step: task 1 survivor 2`.\n- In `task-1-mutants.md` I added a row for the new case and listed the new test as one of mutant 2's targets.\n- A screen run then caught all 3 mutants.\n- Checking the tests against the code from before the task: the test file can't load without `bills`, so all three tests fail there. That step needed no further change.\n- The last full run, at HEAD, caught 3 of 3 with no survivors and no invalid mutants (`.sdd/plan/task-1-mutants-2.log`).\n\n**Completion.** `task-done` ran the project test command, `/private/tmp/msr104-venv/bin/python -m pytest -q`, and all 3 tests passed. It wrote this line to the ledger:\n`Task 1: complete (commits 9dae9f6..18613bd, mutants: 3/3, tests: \u2026 \u2192 3 passed in 0.00s)`\n\nI stopped there and did not start the final review.",
